Sure! One programming problem related to dynamic programming is the Longest Common Substring (LCS) problem. The LCS problem involves finding the longest substring that occurs in at least two given strings. For example, if we have two strings "AGBCAD" and "HDCCBA", the longest substring that occurs in both is "BCADA".

To solve this problem using dynamic programming, we can use a bottom-up approach where we build the solutions to smaller subproblems and use them to solve larger problems.

1. Initialize a table with dimensions corresponding to the lengths of the two given strings. The table will have rows and columns equal to the lengths of the first and second string, respectively.
2. Set a variable to store the maximum length of the longest substring.
3. Iterate through the table, starting from the top-left corner and moving to the bottom-right corner.
4. For each entry in the table, check if the corresponding characters in the two strings are equal. If they are, update the table entry to contain the substring [i, j], where i and j represent the current row and column indices.
5. Check if the updated substring is longer than the current maximum length. If it is, update the maximum length and the substring details.
6. Repeat steps 3 through 5 for all entries in the table.

Here's an example implementation in Java:

    public static String findLCS(String str1, String str2) {
        int[][] dp = new int[str1.length() + 1][str2.length() + 1];
        int maxLength = 0;

        for (int i = 1; i < dp.length; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j < dp[i].length; j++) {
                int currentIndex = i - 1;
                int prevIndex = j - 1;
                if (str1.charAt(currentIndex) == str2.charAt(prevIndex)) {
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1;
                    maxLength = Math.max(maxLength, dp[i][j]);
                } else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);
                }
            }
        }

        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
        int i = maxLength;
        int j = maxLength;
        while (i > 0 && j > 0) {
            if (dp[i - 1][j] == dp[i][j]) {
